<Reading title="About Heliocodex" path="/about" description="Who runs Heliocodex, what it is for, where its facts come from, and how to reach us with a correction or a question.">
  <header class="reading-head">
    <p class="label">About</p>
    <h1>About Heliocodex</h1>
    <p class="lead">A place to look up the Sun, its worlds and the stars, learn how they work, and fly out to them in 3D.</p>
  </header>
  <section class="row">
    <div class="hang"><h2>What it is</h2></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Heliocodex is a space reference. You can look a world or a star up and get one page with its measurements beside its photograph. You can read lessons that start with a first look and go as deep as the physics. And you can leave the page and fly to the same object in 3D, at its true size and distance.</p>
      <p>It is for anyone curious about space: readers of any age, students and amateur astronomers. It is free, shows no adverts and has no accounts.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="row">
    <div class="hang"><h2>Where the facts come from</h2></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Every figure is traced to a named source, and every picture is credited with its licence. Orbits and radii come from NASA and JPL, the stars from a published catalogue, and photographs from the space agencies and observatories that took them. Where something is a drawing or a model rather than a photograph, the caption says so.</p>
      <p>The full list is on <a href="/sources">Sources</a>, and each picture’s credit is on <a href="/licences">Licences and credits</a>. Heliocodex is independent of NASA, ESA and every mission it names, and none of them endorses it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="row">
    <div class="hang"><h2>Who runs it</h2></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Heliocodex is run by FALLINGHIPPO LIMITED, which trades as FallingHippo, a software company. The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> and the <a href="/terms">terms</a> give the company’s details and say how your data is handled.</p>
      <p>The site is built with Astro and three.js. What it keeps in your browser is listed on the <a href="/cookies">cookies and storage page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="row">
    <div class="hang"><h2>Get in touch</h2></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>To report a mistake, if a page does not work for you, or if you need help using it, write to <a href="mailto:support@fallinghippo.com">support@fallinghippo.com</a>, or use the "Report a mistake" link at the foot of the page. Please say which page you were on and what you expected. To ask about reusing something, or to tell us about anything else, write to <a href="mailto:hello@fallinghippo.com">hello@fallinghippo.com</a>.</p>
      <p>Short answers to common questions are on the <a href="/help">questions and answers page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Reading>
